Steps to create it in Scene Builder
Open JavaFX Scene Builder and create a new FXML document.
Drag a VBox from the Containers section onto the layout.
Drag a Label into the VBox and set its text to Hello, JavaFX!.
Drag an ImageView into the VBox.
In the ImageView properties, select an image file and adjust its fit width and fit height.
Set the VBox alignment to CENTER and adjust spacing between elements.
Save the layout as an FXML file.
Result: A JavaFX window displaying a text label and an image using the Label and ImageView controls, respectively.

